---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Close from '../components/Close.astro';
import { applications } from '../data/applications.mjs';
import { site } from '../site.config.mjs';

const files = import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>('../assets/amsoil/*.jpg', { eager: true });
const img = (name: string) => files[`../assets/amsoil/${name}.jpg`].default;

const notes = (await getCollection('notes')).sort(
  (a, b) => b.data.published.valueOf() - a.data.published.valueOf(),
);
---

<Base
  title={`Independent AMSOIL Dealer in ${site.city}, ${site.regionName} | ${site.shortName}`}
  description={site.description}
>
  <section class="sheet">
    <img class="sheet-map" src="/topo.svg" alt="" width="2400" height="1200" fetchpriority="high" />
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="title-block">
        <h1>
          <b>Run it hard.</b>
          <b>Make it last.</b>
          <span>Independent AMSOIL Dealer · {site.city}, {site.regionName}</span>
        </h1>
        <p>
          {site.shortName} is an independent AMSOIL dealership in {site.city}, {site.regionName},
          run by a heavy equipment operator, mechanic and racer. You get a straight answer about
          what your machine needs from someone who has run one like it.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Talk to the dealer</a>
          <a class="more" href="/field-notes/">Read the field notes</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <h2>The oil aisle can’t tell you what your machine needs.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          You paid real money for the machine. Maybe it earns your living on a job site. Maybe it
          carries your name at the track. Either way, it runs hotter, harder and longer than
          anything the bottle on the store shelf was written for.
        </p>
        <p>
          So you guess. You buy what you bought last time, or what the shop next door uses, and
          hope it holds. Nobody at the big-box store can tell you whether it will, because nobody
          there has run your machine.
        </p>
        <p>
          A machine you depend on deserves better than a guess. That is the whole reason this
          dealership exists.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--woodland">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>I’ve run them, wrenched on them and raced them.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          I became a dealer because the work I have done my whole life is the work these products
          are made for. When you describe your machine and your problem, I have usually stood where
          you are standing.
        </p>
        <p><a class="more" href="/about/">More about the dealer</a></p>
      </div>
      <dl class="record">
        <div>
          <dt>Heavy equipment</dt>
          <dd>
            More than a decade as an operator, from small powered equipment to large construction
            machines.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Mechanic</dt>
          <dd>Hands-on repair across most types of machine, and every kind of lubricant in them.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Marine</dt>
          <dd>Certified in marine engines.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Racing</dt>
          <dd>Years in off-road, motocross and drag racing, plus street bikes.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Three kinds of work, one standard.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Different machines fail in different ways. Pick the one closest to yours.
      </p>
      <ul class="legend">
        {
          applications.map((app) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`/applications/${app.slug}/`}>
                <span class="plate">
                  <Image src={img(app.plate)} alt="" height={240} />
                </span>
                <h3>{app.name}</h3>
                <p>
                  {app.summary}
                  <span class="machines">{app.machines}</span>
                </p>
                <span class="go">See {app.name.toLowerCase()}</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>How working with me goes.</h2>
      <ol class="plan">
        <li>
          <h3>Tell me what you run</h3>
          <p>
            The machine, the hours, the conditions, and what has gone wrong before. A call, a text
            or an email is enough.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Get a straight recommendation</h3>
          <p>
            I match the right product to the specification in your manual and to how you actually
            use the machine, and I tell you why.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Run it with confidence</h3>
          <p>
            You order through AMSOIL, and you have a real person to call when you add a machine or
            something changes.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--woodland">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <h2>It costs more per quart. It can cost less per hour.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          AMSOIL has a reputation for being expensive. In my own experience the higher price up
          front mostly disappears once you account for longer service intervals: fewer oil changes,
          fewer filters, and fewer hours with the machine parked.
        </p>
        <p>
          The honest way to compare oils is cost per operating hour, not price per quart. I will
          walk you through that math for your machine, and I will tell you when the cheaper oil is
          the right call.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="more" href="/field-notes/is-synthetic-oil-worth-the-cost/"
            >How to work out oil cost per hour</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Field notes on oil.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Plain answers to the questions operators, riders and shop owners ask most.
      </p>
      <ul class="notes">
        {
          notes.map((note) => (
            <li>
              <h3>
                <a href={`/field-notes/${note.id}/`}>{note.data.title}</a>
              </h3>
              <p>{note.data.answer}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Close />
</Base>
